 "meta": {
  "category": "Technique",
  "level": 3,
  "character": "simple 4/4 with a moving filter",
  "technique": "filter cutoff as the only thing that changes: stepped sweeps by p-lock and smooth sweeps by LFO",
  "secondary": [
   "LFO amount used as a per-hit switch",
   "tempo-synced triangle LFOs (1/1 on the bass, 1/2 on the hat)",
   "a locked parameter must not also be an LFO target"
  ],
  "voices": "Kick, clap: plain. Drum 3 and Drum 2: the same saw bass with resonant low-pass (Drum 3 locked, Drum 2 LFO). Hat: driven, high-pass, LFO amount 0 in the kit.",
  "key": "G (bass G1)",
  "bpm": 124,
  "demonstrates": "Filter modulation makes movement without changing the rhythm: A is static, B moves the bass cutoff by a p-lock on every step (up, then down over two bars), C plays the same bass line on a twin voice whose cutoff an LFO sweeps smoothly, and the hats' high-pass is swept too (the locks only switch the LFOs on).",
  "patterns": [
   "A: static (every cutoff constant)",
   "B: bass cutoff locked step by step (stepped sweep)",
   "C: same line on the LFO twin voice, LFO switched on per hit"
